{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.PhiQWkbGreensFunction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.PhiQWkbGreensFunction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogarithmArchimedeanLimit"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.wkbGreensFunction_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.wkbGreensFunction_zero","kind":"instance","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/phi-q-wkb-greens-function.lean#L118-L133","doc":"**Unconditional instance at `x = 0`.** Both `nextOrderCorrection q\n0 n` and `diracLogDet 0` are identically zero by the boundary\naxioms, so the limit is the constant zero sequence. This is the\nonly point at which the `WKBGreensFunction` class can be\ninhabited without further Mathlib infrastructure; for every\n`x ∈ (0, 1)` the instance requires stationary-phase asymptotics\nand heat-kernel determinant theory. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.nextOrderCorrection_to_diracLogDet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.nextOrderCorrection_to_diracLogDet","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/phi-q-wkb-greens-function.lean#L108-L116","doc":"Stated form of the conjecture (sorry-free at the level of Lean,\ninhabited only via a `[WKBGreensFunction x]` typeclass instance). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.WKBGreensFunction.one_loop_determinant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.WKBGreensFunction.one_loop_determinant","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/phi-q-wkb-greens-function.lean#L102-L102","doc":"The Faddeev `ℏ_q⁰` correction equals the half-log-determinant\nof the categorical Dirac operator at the dominant saddle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.WKBGreensFunction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.WKBGreensFunction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/phi-q-wkb-greens-function.lean#L98-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.WKBGreensFunction.toArchimedeanLimit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.WKBGreensFunction.toArchimedeanLimit","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/phi-q-wkb-greens-function.lean#L98-L106","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.WKBGreensFunction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.WKBGreensFunction","kind":"class","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/phi-q-wkb-greens-function.lean#L92-L106","doc":"The next-order Faddeev-WKB conjecture, packaged as a typeclass.\nA concrete instance asserts that, in addition to the leading-\norder Li₂ convergence (encoded by the parent class\n`ArchimedeanLimit x`), the `ℏ_q⁰` correction converges to\n`diracLogDet x` along Faddeev's joint scaling. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:phi-q-wkb-greens-function","label":"conj:phi-q-wkb-greens-function","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/phi-q-wkb-greens-function.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.nextOrderCorrection_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.nextOrderCorrection_zero","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/phi-q-wkb-greens-function.lean#L85-L90","doc":"Boundary lemma: at `x = 0` the next-order correction is zero.\n**Was an axiom; now a projection (2026-09-04)** — see the note on\n`diracLogDetAux`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.diracLogDet_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.diracLogDet_zero","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/phi-q-wkb-greens-function.lean#L78-L83","doc":"Boundary lemma: at `x = 0` the half-log-determinant placeholder is zero.\n**Was an axiom; now a projection (2026-09-04)** — see the note on\n`diracLogDetAux`. Built into the opaque interface exactly as before, but\nby construction rather than by assumption. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.nextOrderCorrection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.nextOrderCorrection","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/phi-q-wkb-greens-function.lean#L75-L76","doc":"The next-to-leading-order Faddeev residual itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.nextOrderCorrectionAux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.nextOrderCorrectionAux","kind":"opaque","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/phi-q-wkb-greens-function.lean#L66-L73","doc":"Opaque placeholder for the next-to-leading-order Faddeev residual,\ni.e. the `ℏ_q⁰` term of `log Φ_n(x; q) - ℏ_q⁻¹ Li₂(x)` as\n`q → 1`, `n → ∞`, `n(1-q) → ∞`. Concrete formulation requires\na stationary-phase development with uniform error bounds; this\nopaque stub lets the conjecture statement compile. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.diracLogDet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.diracLogDet","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/phi-q-wkb-greens-function.lean#L63-L64","doc":"The half-log-determinant placeholder itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.diracLogDetAux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.diracLogDetAux","kind":"opaque","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/phi-q-wkb-greens-function.lean#L45-L61","doc":"Opaque placeholder for `-½ log det 𝔇_∇|_{x₀}`. The half-log-\ndeterminant of the categorical Dirac operator at the dominant\nsaddle x₀ of the Faddeev WKB expansion. Concrete definition\nrequires heat-kernel / zeta-function determinant theory (not yet\nin Mathlib); this opaque stub lets the conjecture statement\ncompile. ","signatureChunk":0}]}